# Higher-Order Decision Architect (router)

Before **material coding decisions** (architecture, dependencies, public API, security, data contracts, multi-module refactors, or anything hard to revert):

1. Load and follow [higher-order-decision-architect/SKILL.md](../higher-order-decision-architect/SKILL.md).
2. Run the mental-model sequence **internally** on every such decision — all **8 steps**, including **thrive ascent (2036)** after honest pre-mortem.
3. For **non-trivial** choices, surface **Executive Verdict**, **risks**, **thrive ascent**, **confidence**, and **next actions** (full template in the skill — do not paste the entire block on trivial edits).

**Thrive counterweight:** pre-mortem is honest; step 8 reframes risk as trajectory guardrails (refuse vs build toward horizon). Never end on defeat without an acceleration alternative.

Project-specific hooks (e.g. WASM/metre contracts, shell kernel/plugin) live in skill overlays — e.g. [examples/overlays/thepulimaangani-decision-hooks.md](../examples/overlays/thepulimaangani-decision-hooks.md) or `~/.config/shell/arch-design/overlays/shell-kernel-decision-hooks.md`.

This rule governs **how** to decide; it does not replace language, test commands, or verification steps in project `AGENTS.md`.
